@lang en
IMPORT `law36-art88-89-transitional`

-- Law 36/2024/QH15 on alcohol, drugs and stimulants: Article 9(2)-(3) (the prohibitions),
-- Articles 81(3) and 83(2)(a) (testing after an accident), Article 87(5) (the Ministry of
-- Health determines alcohol and endogenous alcohol in blood).
-- Decree 67/2023 Article 7(2)(đ) excludes damage to property caused by a driver whose blood or
-- breath alcohol "exceeds the normal value in the guidance of the Ministry of Health", or who
-- used drugs or stimulants the law prohibits (Decree 67 src 225-227, in VN-10's rendering; its
-- Vietnamese is not quoted here because it is not in this row's sources).
--
-- What this Law says:
-- * Article 9(2): driving with any alcohol concentration in the blood or breath is prohibited.
--   There is no permitted level above zero.
-- * Article 9(3): driving with a narcotic or another prohibited stimulant in the body is
--   prohibited; there is no level either.
-- * Article 87(5): the Ministry of Health regulates "xác định nồng độ cồn và nồng độ cồn nội
--   sinh trong máu" (determining the alcohol concentration and the endogenous alcohol
--   concentration in blood). Endogenous alcohol is the body's own; the Law does not say how
--   much there may be, and says it of blood only.

§ `Alcohol, drugs and stimulants`

§§ `Article 9(2)-(3) — the prohibitions`

-- src:law36-2024-qh15-977-978:233 | Điều 9. Các hành vi bị nghiêm cấm
-- src:law36-2024-qh15-977-978:238 | 2. Điều khiển phương tiện tham gia giao thông đường bộ mà trong máu hoặc
-- src:law36-2024-qh15-977-978:239 | hơi thở có nồng độ cồn.
-- src:law36-2024-qh15-977-978:240 | 3. Điều khiển phương tiện tham gia giao thông đường bộ mà trong cơ thể có
-- src:law36-2024-qh15-977-978:241 | chất ma túy hoặc chất kích thích khác mà pháp luật cấm sử dụng.

-- Article 9(2): the level of alcohol the Law permits a driver is none.
@ref Law 36/2024/QH15 Article 9(2)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the permitted level of alcohol under the Law` MEANS 0

-- Article 87(5): alcohol in the blood that the Ministry of Health's method finds endogenous.
-- src:1934 | 5. Bộ Y tế thực hiện quản lý nhà nước về điều kiện sức khỏe của người lái xe,
-- src:1935 | người điều khiển xe máy chuyên dùng tham gia giao thông đường bộ; quy định về
-- src:1936 | xác định nồng độ cồn và nồng độ cồn nội sinh trong máu.
@ref Law 36/2024/QH15 Article 87(5)
GIVEN t IS A `A test of the driver`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 87(5) — the alcohol in the blood was found endogenous` t MEANS
        t's `medium` EQUALS `blood`
    AND t's `found endogenous by the Ministry of Health's method` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Article 9(2): the driver drove with alcohol in the blood or breath. Fork F28: alcohol in the
-- blood that the Ministry of Health's method found endogenous (Article 87(5)) is not the
-- alcohol 9(2) forbids. Fork F29: a reading above zero with no such finding is.
@ref Law 36/2024/QH15 Article 9(2), 87(5)
GIVEN t IS A `A test of the driver`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 9(2) — the test` t `shows driving with alcohol in the blood or breath, on` d MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `Article 88 — this Law governs` d                                      THEN `the Road Traffic Law 23/2008/QH12 governs a day before 1 January 2025, and it is not in the sources`
           IF t's `alcohol concentration found` AT MOST `the permitted level of alcohol under the Law` THEN FALSE
           IF `Article 87(5) — the alcohol in the blood was found endogenous` t                  THEN FALSE
           OTHERWISE                                                                            TRUE

-- Article 9(3), with Article 83(2)(a): a narcotic or another stimulant the law prohibits, in
-- the body. The Law states no level; which substances the law prohibits is for the law on
-- drugs, so the laboratory's finding is the input.
